*> The advanced datamunge::optim classes: ProximalGradient, FISTA, LevenbergMarquardt, Newton,
*> TrustRegionNewton, AugmentedLagrangian, SQP, InteriorPoint, BayesianOptimization and
*> RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate.
*> The optimizers take interfaces (HessianFunction, ResidualFunction, ...) that the C++ library
*> leaves abstract. COBOL implements them through the -EXTEND records: each PROGRAM-POINTER names
*> a program after END PROGRAM OPTIM-ADVANCED-EX that overrides one virtual method. The
*> coordinates are a VECTOR-DOUBLE that the optimizer overwrites with the solution.
*> Run with `just run-cobol TARGET=optim_advanced_ex`.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. OPTIM-ADVANCED-EX.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".

*> Sample points of the bowl y = (x - 1)^2.
01 XS-DATA.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.5.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 1.0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 1.5.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 2.0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 3.0.
01 XS REDEFINES XS-DATA.
   05 XS-ITEM USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 6.
01 PROBE-DATA.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.25.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 1.0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 2.5.
01 PROBES REDEFINES PROBE-DATA.
   05 PROBE-X USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 3.
*> The sample times t of the exponential fit, shared with EXP-RESIDUALS and EXP-JACOBIAN.
01 SAMPLE-TIMES EXTERNAL.
   05 SAMPLE-T  USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 5.

01 SURROGATE    USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 POINTS       USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 VALUES-VEC   USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 PG           USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 FISTA        USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 LM           USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 NEWTON       USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 TRN          USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 AL           USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 SQP          USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 IP           USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 BO           USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 OBJECTIVE    USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 COORDS        USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 LABEL-TEXT   PIC X(24).
01 INCUMBENT    USAGE COMP-2.
01 Y-VALUE      USAGE COMP-2.
01 I            USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 X-TEXT       PIC 9.99.
01 FIXED-TEXT   PIC -(4)9.9(6).
01 FIXED-TEXT-2 PIC -(4)9.9(6).
01 MENTIONS-GRADIENT USAGE BINARY-LONG.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    DISPLAY "=================== RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate (concrete BayesianSurrogate) ==================="
    *> Fit a 1D surrogate to the bowl sampled at a few points, then check that the
    *> acquisition function favors an unexplored region.
    MOVE 2 TO DM-RBF-GSSN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-NEW-DOUBLE-DOUBLE-GIVEN
    MOVE 1.0 TO DM-RBF-GSSN-PRCSS-SRRGT-NEW-DOUBLE-DOUBLE-LENGTH-SCALE
    MOVE 1.0E-6 TO DM-RBF-GSSN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-NEW-DOUBLE-DOUBLE-NOISE
    CALL "dm_rbf_gaussian_process_surrogate_new_double_double"
        USING DM-RBF-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-NEW-DOUBLE-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-RBF-GSSN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-NEW-DOUBLE-DOUBLE-RESULT TO SURROGATE
    *> points: one single-coordinate row per sample; values: (x - 1)^2.
    CALL "dm_vector_vector_double_new" USING DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SELF TO POINTS
    MOVE 6 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 6
        COMPUTE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(I) = (XS-ITEM(I) - 1.0) ** 2
        CALL "dm_vector_double_new" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
        MOVE XS-ITEM(I) TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE
        CALL "dm_vector_double_push" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
        MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SELF TO DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE DM-HANDLE-SELF
        CALL "dm_vector_vector_double_push" USING DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
        PERFORM CHECK
        CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    END-PERFORM
    CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO VALUES-VEC
    MOVE SURROGATE TO DM-RBF-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-FIT-SELF
    MOVE POINTS TO DM-RBF-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-FIT-POINTS
    MOVE VALUES-VEC TO DM-RBF-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-FIT-VALUES
    CALL "dm_rbf_gaussian_process_surrogate_fit" USING DM-RBF-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-FIT DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK

    *> The best observed value so far (the minimum of the values).
    MOVE 0.0 TO INCUMBENT
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 6
        IF DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(I) < INCUMBENT
            MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(I) TO INCUMBENT
        END-IF
    END-PERFORM
    DISPLAY "incumbent (best observed y): " INCUMBENT
    MOVE SURROGATE TO DM-RBF-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-ACQUISITION-SELF
    MOVE INCUMBENT TO DM-RBF-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-ACQUISITION-INCUMBENT
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 3
        CALL "dm_vector_double_new" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
        MOVE PROBE-X(I) TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE
        CALL "dm_vector_double_push" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
        MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SELF TO DM-RBF-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-ACQUISITION-POINT
        CALL "dm_rbf_gaussian_process_surrogate_acquisition"
            USING DM-RBF-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-ACQUISITION DM-STATUS
        PERFORM CHECK
        COMPUTE X-TEXT ROUNDED = PROBE-X(I)
        COMPUTE FIXED-TEXT ROUNDED = DM-RBF-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-SURROGATE-ACQUISITION-RESULT
        DISPLAY "acquisition(x=" X-TEXT ") = " FUNCTION TRIM(FIXED-TEXT)
        MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SELF TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
        CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    END-PERFORM

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "=================== Options structs + optimizer construction (all 10 new classes) ==================="
    *> Every new Options struct and optimizer class constructs cleanly; each line shows the handle's type.
    CALL "dm_proximal_gradient_options_new" USING DM-PROXIMAL-GRADIENT-OPTIONS-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-PROXIMAL-GRADIENT-OPTIONS-NEW-RESULT TO OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS DM-PROXIMAL-GRADIENT-OPTIONS-STEP-SIZE-SELF
    MOVE 0.05 TO DM-PROXIMAL-GRADIENT-OPTIONS-STEP-SIZE-VALUE
    CALL "dm_proximal_gradient_options_step_size_set" USING DM-PROXIMAL-GRADIENT-OPTIONS-STEP-SIZE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE 1 TO DM-PROXIMAL-GRADIENT-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS TO DM-PROXIMAL-GRADIENT-NEW-OPTIONS
    CALL "dm_proximal_gradient_new" USING DM-PROXIMAL-GRADIENT-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-PROXIMAL-GRADIENT-NEW-RESULT TO PG DM-HANDLE-SELF
    MOVE "ProximalGradient: " TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM SHOW-HANDLE

    CALL "dm_fista_options_new" USING DM-FISTA-OPTIONS-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE 1 TO DM-FISTA-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE DM-FISTA-OPTIONS-NEW-RESULT TO OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS DM-FISTA-NEW-OPTIONS
    CALL "dm_fista_new" USING DM-FISTA-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-FISTA-NEW-RESULT TO FISTA DM-HANDLE-SELF
    MOVE "FISTA: " TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM SHOW-HANDLE

    CALL "dm_levenberg_marquardt_options_new" USING DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-OPTIONS-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-OPTIONS-NEW-RESULT TO OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS
        DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-OPTIONS-MAX-ITERATIONS-SELF
    MOVE 200 TO DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-OPTIONS-MAX-ITERATIONS-VALUE
    CALL "dm_levenberg_marquardt_options_max_iterations_set"
        USING DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-OPTIONS-MAX-ITERATIONS DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE 1 TO DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS TO DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-NEW-OPTIONS
    CALL "dm_levenberg_marquardt_new" USING DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-NEW-RESULT TO LM DM-HANDLE-SELF
    MOVE "LevenbergMarquardt: " TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM SHOW-HANDLE

    CALL "dm_newton_options_new" USING DM-NEWTON-OPTIONS-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE 1 TO DM-NEWTON-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE DM-NEWTON-OPTIONS-NEW-RESULT TO OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS DM-NEWTON-NEW-OPTIONS
    CALL "dm_newton_new" USING DM-NEWTON-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-NEWTON-NEW-RESULT TO NEWTON DM-HANDLE-SELF
    MOVE "Newton: " TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM SHOW-HANDLE

    CALL "dm_trust_region_newton_options_new" USING DM-TRUST-REGION-NEWTON-OPTIONS-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE 1 TO DM-TRUST-REGION-NEWTON-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE DM-TRUST-REGION-NEWTON-OPTIONS-NEW-RESULT TO OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS DM-TRUST-REGION-NEWTON-NEW-OPTIONS
    CALL "dm_trust_region_newton_new" USING DM-TRUST-REGION-NEWTON-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-TRUST-REGION-NEWTON-NEW-RESULT TO TRN DM-HANDLE-SELF
    MOVE "TrustRegionNewton: " TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM SHOW-HANDLE

    CALL "dm_augmented_lagrangian_options_new" USING DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIONS-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE 1 TO DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIONS-NEW-RESULT TO OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS
        DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-NEW-OPTIONS
    CALL "dm_augmented_lagrangian_new" USING DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-NEW-RESULT TO AL DM-HANDLE-SELF
    MOVE "AugmentedLagrangian: " TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM SHOW-HANDLE

    CALL "dm_sqp_options_new" USING DM-SQP-OPTIONS-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE 1 TO DM-SQP-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE DM-SQP-OPTIONS-NEW-RESULT TO OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS DM-SQP-NEW-OPTIONS
    CALL "dm_sqp_new" USING DM-SQP-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-SQP-NEW-RESULT TO SQP DM-HANDLE-SELF
    MOVE "SQP: " TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM SHOW-HANDLE

    CALL "dm_interior_point_options_new" USING DM-INTERIOR-POINT-OPTIONS-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE 1 TO DM-INTERIOR-POINT-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE DM-INTERIOR-POINT-OPTIONS-NEW-RESULT TO OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS DM-INTERIOR-POINT-NEW-OPTIONS
    CALL "dm_interior_point_new" USING DM-INTERIOR-POINT-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-INTERIOR-POINT-NEW-RESULT TO IP DM-HANDLE-SELF
    MOVE "InteriorPoint: " TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM SHOW-HANDLE

    CALL "dm_bayesian_optimization_options_new" USING DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIONS-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIONS-NEW-RESULT TO OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS
        DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIONS-INITIAL-SAMPLES-SELF
    MOVE 8 TO DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIONS-INITIAL-SAMPLES-VALUE
    CALL "dm_bayesian_optimization_options_initial_samples_set"
        USING DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIONS-INITIAL-SAMPLES DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE 1 TO DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS TO DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-NEW-OPTIONS
    CALL "dm_bayesian_optimization_new" USING DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-NEW-RESULT TO BO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    MOVE "BayesianOptimization: " TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM SHOW-HANDLE

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "=================== COBOL objectives (overriding the C++ interfaces) ==================="
    *> Newton's method on f(x, y) = (x - 1)^2 + 10 (y + 2)^2 with exact gradient and Hessian.
    SET DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EXTEND-EVALUATE TO ENTRY "QUAD-EVALUATE"
    SET DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EXTEND-GRADIENT TO ENTRY "QUAD-GRADIENT"
    SET DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EXTEND-HESSIAN TO ENTRY "QUAD-HESSIAN"
    CALL "dm_hessian_function_extend" USING DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EXTEND DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EXTEND-RESULT TO OBJECTIVE
    MOVE 2 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    MOVE 5.0 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1) DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2)
    CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO COORDS
    MOVE NEWTON TO DM-NEWTON-OPTIMIZE-SELF
    MOVE OBJECTIVE TO DM-NEWTON-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION
    MOVE COORDS TO DM-NEWTON-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES
    CALL "dm_newton_optimize" USING DM-NEWTON-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    PERFORM READ-COORDS
    COMPUTE FIXED-TEXT ROUNDED = DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1)
    COMPUTE FIXED-TEXT-2 ROUNDED = DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2)
    DISPLAY "Newton: f = " DM-NEWTON-OPTIMIZE-RESULT " at (" FUNCTION TRIM(FIXED-TEXT) ", "
        FUNCTION TRIM(FIXED-TEXT-2) ") (exact minimum 0 at (1, -2))"

    *> Levenberg-Marquardt fitting y = a * exp(b t) to exact data from a = 2, b = 0.5.
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 5
        COMPUTE SAMPLE-T(I) = (I - 1) * 0.5
    END-PERFORM
    SET DM-RESIDUAL-FUNCTION-EXTEND-RESIDUALS TO ENTRY "EXP-RESIDUALS"
    SET DM-RESIDUAL-FUNCTION-EXTEND-JACOBIAN TO ENTRY "EXP-JACOBIAN"
    CALL "dm_residual_function_extend" USING DM-RESIDUAL-FUNCTION-EXTEND DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE 2 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    MOVE 1.0 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1)
    MOVE 0.1 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2)
    CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO COORDS
    MOVE LM TO DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-OPTIMIZE-SELF
    MOVE DM-RESIDUAL-FUNCTION-EXTEND-RESULT TO DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION
    MOVE COORDS TO DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES
    CALL "dm_levenberg_marquardt_optimize" USING DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    PERFORM READ-COORDS
    COMPUTE FIXED-TEXT ROUNDED = DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1)
    COMPUTE FIXED-TEXT-2 ROUNDED = DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2)
    DISPLAY "LevenbergMarquardt: residual = " DM-LEVENBERG-MARQUARDT-OPTIMIZE-RESULT
        ", a = " FUNCTION TRIM(FIXED-TEXT) ", b = " FUNCTION TRIM(FIXED-TEXT-2) " (exact: 2, 0.5)"

    *> An override a subclass leaves out: a HessianFunction without gradient(). COBOL refuses it
    *> when the subclass is made, before any optimizer can call it.
    SET DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EXTEND-EVALUATE TO ENTRY "INCOMPLETE-EVALUATE"
    SET DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EXTEND-GRADIENT TO NULL
    CALL "dm_hessian_function_extend" USING DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EXTEND DM-STATUS
    IF DM-STATUS-OK
        MOVE DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EXTEND-RESULT TO DM-NEWTON-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION
        CALL "dm_newton_optimize" USING DM-NEWTON-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
    END-IF
    MOVE 0 TO MENTIONS-GRADIENT
    IF NOT DM-STATUS-OK
        INSPECT DM-STATUS-MESSAGE(1:DM-STATUS-LENGTH) TALLYING MENTIONS-GRADIENT FOR ALL "gradient"
    END-IF
    IF DM-STATUS-OK
        DISPLAY "missing gradient(): ok=true, error mentions it: false"
    ELSE
        IF MENTIONS-GRADIENT > 0
            DISPLAY "missing gradient(): ok=false, error mentions it: true"
        ELSE
            DISPLAY "missing gradient(): ok=false, error mentions it: false"
        END-IF
    END-IF
    *> The failed call above left its error kind in RETURN-CODE.
    MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    STOP RUN.

*> Displays LABEL-TEXT and the type of the handle in DM-HANDLE-SELF.
SHOW-HANDLE.
    CALL "dm_handle_type" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    DISPLAY FUNCTION TRIM(LABEL-TEXT TRAILING) " " DM-HANDLE-TYPE(1:DM-HANDLE-TYPE-LENGTH) " handle".

*> Copies the coordinates in COORDS (as left by an optimizer) into the VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE items.
READ-COORDS.
    MOVE COORDS TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF
    MOVE 1 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-START
    CALL "dm_vector_double_to_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK.

*> Stops with the error after a failed call.
CHECK.
    IF NOT DM-STATUS-OK
        DISPLAY "datamunge error (" FUNCTION TRIM(DM-STATUS-KIND) "): "
            DM-STATUS-MESSAGE(1:DM-STATUS-LENGTH) UPON SYSERR
        STOP RUN RETURNING 1
    END-IF.
END PROGRAM OPTIM-ADVANCED-EX.

*> HessianFunction::evaluate: f(x, y) = (x - 1)^2 + 10 (y + 2)^2.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. QUAD-EVALUATE.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".
LINKAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge-callbacks.cpy".
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EVALUATE-ARGS DM-CALLBACK-STATUS.
    MOVE DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EVALUATE-ARGS-COORDINATES TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_vector_double_to_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    COMPUTE DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EVALUATE-ARGS-RESULT =
        (DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1) - 1) ** 2 + 10 * (DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2) + 2) ** 2
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM QUAD-EVALUATE.

*> HessianFunction::gradient: (2 (x - 1), 20 (y + 2)), as a new vector.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. QUAD-GRADIENT.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".
01 X USAGE COMP-2.
01 Y USAGE COMP-2.
LINKAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge-callbacks.cpy".
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-GRADIENT-ARGS DM-CALLBACK-STATUS.
    MOVE DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-GRADIENT-ARGS-COORDINATES TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_vector_double_to_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1) TO X
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2) TO Y
    COMPUTE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1) = 2 * (X - 1)
    COMPUTE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2) = 20 * (Y + 2)
    CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    *> C++ takes the returned vector and closes its handle.
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-GRADIENT-ARGS-RESULT
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM QUAD-GRADIENT.

*> HessianFunction::hessian: the constant matrix ((2, 0), (0, 20)).
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. QUAD-HESSIAN.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".
LINKAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge-callbacks.cpy".
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-HESSIAN-ARGS DM-CALLBACK-STATUS.
    CALL "dm_vector_vector_double_new" USING DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE 2 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    MOVE 2.0 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1)
    MOVE 0.0 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2)
    PERFORM PUSH-ROW
    MOVE 0.0 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1)
    MOVE 20.0 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2)
    PERFORM PUSH-ROW
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SELF TO DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-HESSIAN-ARGS-RESULT
    GOBACK.

*> Appends the table items as one row (push copies it, so the row vector is closed).
PUSH-ROW.
    CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_vector_vector_double_push" USING DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS.
END PROGRAM QUAD-HESSIAN.

*> ResidualFunction::residuals: a exp(b t) - 2 exp(0.5 t) at each sample time.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. EXP-RESIDUALS.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".
01 SAMPLE-TIMES EXTERNAL.
   05 SAMPLE-T  USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 5.
01 A            USAGE COMP-2.
01 B            USAGE COMP-2.
01 I            USAGE BINARY-LONG.
LINKAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge-callbacks.cpy".
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING DM-RESIDUAL-FUNCTION-RESIDUALS-ARGS DM-CALLBACK-STATUS.
    MOVE DM-RESIDUAL-FUNCTION-RESIDUALS-ARGS-COORDINATES TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_vector_double_to_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1) TO A
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2) TO B
    MOVE 5 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 5
        COMPUTE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(I) =
            A * FUNCTION EXP(B * SAMPLE-T(I)) - 2 * FUNCTION EXP(0.5 * SAMPLE-T(I))
    END-PERFORM
    CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO DM-RESIDUAL-FUNCTION-RESIDUALS-ARGS-RESULT
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM EXP-RESIDUALS.

*> ResidualFunction::jacobian: rows (exp(b t), a t exp(b t)).
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. EXP-JACOBIAN.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".
01 SAMPLE-TIMES EXTERNAL.
   05 SAMPLE-T  USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 5.
01 A            USAGE COMP-2.
01 B            USAGE COMP-2.
01 I            USAGE BINARY-LONG.
LINKAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge-callbacks.cpy".
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING DM-RESIDUAL-FUNCTION-JACOBIAN-ARGS DM-CALLBACK-STATUS.
    MOVE DM-RESIDUAL-FUNCTION-JACOBIAN-ARGS-COORDINATES TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_vector_double_to_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1) TO A
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2) TO B
    CALL "dm_vector_vector_double_new" USING DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE 2 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 5
        COMPUTE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1) = FUNCTION EXP(B * SAMPLE-T(I))
        COMPUTE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2) = A * SAMPLE-T(I) * FUNCTION EXP(B * SAMPLE-T(I))
        CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
        MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE DM-HANDLE-SELF
        CALL "dm_vector_vector_double_push" USING DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
        CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SELF TO DM-RESIDUAL-FUNCTION-JACOBIAN-ARGS-RESULT
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM EXP-JACOBIAN.

*> HessianFunction::evaluate of the incomplete objective: always 0.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. INCOMPLETE-EVALUATE.
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge-callbacks.cpy".
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EVALUATE-ARGS DM-CALLBACK-STATUS.
    MOVE 0 TO DM-HESSIAN-FUNCTION-EVALUATE-ARGS-RESULT
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM INCOMPLETE-EVALUATE.
